Fix: corpus materialization progress display
Date: 2026-08-16
Branch: fix/corpus-progress-display
Baseline: 83b78a4 (main)

DEFECT (from desktop QA 2026-08-16, 18 PASS / 1 FAIL / 1 NOT EXECUTED)
`corpus_first_run_materialization` FAIL: materialization completed and rendered
`corpus-facts`, but no progress was shown at any point. Rust `fetch_corpus` does
report progress step by step through `Channel<Event<CorpusProgress, Value>>`
(crates/yunjian-app/src/ipc.rs), and PR #105 had already created the Channel on
the frontend — but never subscribed `onmessage`, so every event was dropped.
The inline comment admitted it: "设置面板暂不渲染进度".

BACKEND EVENT SHAPE (read from source, not guessed)
- Outer `Event<P, I>` is ADJACENTLY tagged: #[serde(tag="type", content="payload")]
  (crates/yunjian-core/src/operation.rs:14) → progress / item / done / cancelled / failed
- Inner `CorpusProgress` is INTERNALLY tagged: #[serde(tag="stage")]
  (crates/yunjian-app/src/ipc.rs:781), eight variants:
  already_present{path} verifying_archive{archive,bytes} archive_verified{sha256}
  decompressing{bytes_done,bytes_total} materialized{path,corpus_version}
  deriving{...} derive_failed{reason} ready{path,corpus_version,derived}
- Wire form: {type:"progress", payload:{stage:"decompressing", bytes_done, bytes_total}}
- Terminal: Event::Done on success, Event::Failed{message} on error.

BACKEND CHANGE
`CorpusProgress::Deriving` previously carried `detail: format!("{progress:?}")`,
collapsing the kernel's UI-facing `DeriveStep::display_name()` (derive.rs:60) plus
done/total into one Rust debug string. Changed to structured {step, done, total}.

$ cargo check -p yunjian-app
RESULT: PASS

FRONTEND CHANGES
- app/src/contracts/settings.ts: CorpusProgress (8 variants), CORPUS_PROGRESS_LABEL,
  CorpusProgressEvent. Field names copied verbatim from ipc.rs.
- app/src/data/progressChannel.ts (NEW): the single Channel construction point.
  Construction and subscription are one indivisible action.
- app/src/data/settingsPorts.ts: CorpusPort.fetchCorpus(onEvent) — REQUIRED param.
- app/src/data/{sampleSettingsPorts,tauriPorts,sampleVoicePorts}.ts: all routed
  through progressChannel.
- app/src/settings/CorpusPanel.tsx: progress block with role=progressbar, stage
  label, percent, detail line; no aria-valuenow when the denominator is unknown.
- app/src/settings/settings.css: existing tokens only; ratio→width via calc() in
  CSS (noScoreArithmetic.test.ts forbids ratio arithmetic in TS);
  prefers-reduced-motion disables the indeterminate sweep.

ASSERTIONS ADDED (three layers)
1. Behavioral — app/src/data/__tests__/tauriChannelContract.test.ts
   Sends a real event into the handed-over Channel and requires it to reach the
   caller's callback. The pre-existing assertion only asked whether a Channel was
   present in the args, which is exactly why "created but unsubscribed" was green.
2. Structural — app/src/data/__tests__/channelSubscription.test.ts (NEW)
   `new Channel` may appear only in progressChannel.ts; that factory must assign
   `onmessage`; comments and string literals are stripped before scanning, and a
   third test pins the stripping behaviour itself.
3. Rendering — app/src/settings/__tests__/SettingsScreen.test.tsx (7 new)
   Immediate feedback before the first event; MiB + percent while decompressing;
   kernel step name + poem counts while deriving; no 0% when total==0;
   derive_failed is informational, not an error; progress yields to the facts
   table on completion; the "not downloaded" note disappears during the fetch.

INJECTION VERIFICATION (tsc state checked each round before judging red)
a) Removed `channel.onmessage = onEvent;` from progressChannel.ts
   → tsc: TS6133 'onEvent' declared but never read
   → 2 tests FAILED (structural factory check + behavioural delivery check)
b) Reverted; changed sampleSettingsPorts.ts back to a bare `new Channel<unknown>()`
   → tsc: TS6133 on both the unused import and the unused param
   → 2 tests FAILED (construction-site check + behavioural delivery check)
c) Reverted; removed `{busy && <CorpusProgressView …/>}` leaving the comment
   → tsc: TS6133 on `progress` and `CorpusProgressView`
   → 6 tests FAILED (all rendering assertions)
All three restored; `npx tsc --noEmit` clean afterwards.
Note: every round also produced TS6133 — that is the type-layer guard working.

HARNESS CHANGES (xtask/src/acceptance/dom.rs)
- Screenshot the progress block when the FIRST progress text arrives. The
  end-of-run full-window screenshot cannot show progress (the block yields to the
  facts table by design), so without this the PASS had text but no image.
  Falls back to a full-window shot when the element endpoint returns flat colour,
  same escape hatch as record_focused.
- Verdict text now samples the progress texts (first 3 … omitted N … last 3).
  The first run listed all 484 near-identical strings, making that report row too
  long to read — an unread verdict is equivalent to no verdict. The count itself
  stays exact via progress_seen.len().
- 3 unit tests for the sampling helper and the screenshot filename.

